{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-maintained classification for the binding-gaps scan. The scan never",
    "guesses: a name it does not find here lands in the report's 'Unclassified'",
    "section and stays out of the gap counts until someone adds it.",
    "",
    "pkgconfig: pkg-config name -> GI namespace, or null when it is not a",
    "binding target at all (build tooling, a system library with no GObject",
    "introspection, or something a Ruby port would use a plain gem for).",
    "",
    "app_internal: namespaces an app defines for itself. They show up in",
    "gi.require_version calls inside the app and are not libraries to bind.",
    "",
    "platform: namespaces that exist but no Ruby GTK port should ever need -",
    "windowing-system and GPU backends, font stack internals, test doubles.",
    "",
    "rust_gi_crates: the only Cargo dependencies that mean a binding. Every",
    "other crate in a Rust upstream is pure Rust and maps to 'find a Ruby",
    "equivalent', not to a gem that has to be written.",
    "",
    "demo_repos: forks that are collections of sample code rather than one app.",
    "They pull in half of GNOME and would dominate every count, so they are",
    "excluded from app counts and never named as blocked.",
    "",
    "extra_coverage: namespaces ruby-gnome ships that the scan cannot see by",
    "reading loader calls - glib2 binds its namespaces through its C extension,",
    "and rcairo lives outside the ruby-gnome repo entirely. Keep this list as",
    "short as it can be; everything else is discovered at runtime."
  ],
